// v0.3-M1 background timing fixture.
// Verifies that background tasks run on a separate thread: main continues
// before the background task completes.
//
// The background task sleeps 200ms. Main prints `main done` immediately after
// scheduling the task. The test verifies `main done` appears within 50ms
// and `background done` appears after (ordering proves separate-thread scheduling).
//
// NOTE: sleepMs (NOT wait) — `wait` stays synchronous in M1 (state machines ship
// in v0.3-M2). sleepMs is the v0.3-M1 Yinz intrinsic that calls the blocking
// sleep helper on the background thread pool.

function recordEvent() -> nothing {
  sleepMs(200)
  print(`background done`)
}

function entrypoint() -> nothing {
  background recordEvent()
  print(`main done`)
}
